# Web E2E Testing Rules

## Browser Targets

- **Default**: Chromium (all tests)
- **Parallel smoke**: Firefox + WebKit (tagged `@smoke`, 10% of suite)
- Mobile: iPhone 14 viewport (390x844) for critical user flows

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts
projects: [
  { name: 'chromium', use: { browserName: 'chromium' } },
  { name: 'firefox', use: { browserName: 'firefox' } },
  { name: 'webkit', use: { browserName: 'webkit' } },
  { name: 'mobile-chrome', use: { ...devices['Pixel 5'] } },
  { name: 'mobile-safari', use: { ...devices['iPhone 14'] } },
],
```

## Network Interception

- Mock external APIs with `page.route()` — never hit real production APIs
- Assert on network responses when testing loading/error states
- Use `page.waitForResponse()` for mutation operations

## Test Data

- Seed test data through API calls (not UI) in `beforeAll`
- Clean up created data in `afterAll`
- Never hardcode user-specific IDs — query by role/label/text
- Use isolated test accounts or auth tokens

## Reporting

- Always capture trace on retry: `trace: 'on-first-retry'`
- Screenshot on failure: `screenshots: 'only-on-failure'`
- Video on failure: `video: 'retain-on-failure'`
